# ---- state→DB slice 8 (BH-1033) — the two log-as-state stores ----
# BOTH ARE SETTINGS ROWS FIRST and these env values second, and both default to
# OFF. Off is today's behaviour byte for byte: not one extra request, not one
# changed decision. Flip them on a verified deploy with
#   bin/jobs-client.sh setting-set ready_queue_rows 1
#   bin/jobs-client.sh setting-set closeout_aged_table 1
# and roll back by setting the same row to 0 — there is nothing else to undo.
#
# ready_queue_rows: "what is ready to build" is the `ready` build_queue ROWS
# UNION logs/READY-QUEUE.log, instead of that file alone. The file keeps being
# written (it is still the log and still the fallback); the rows are what a box
# other than the one holding the file can see, which is what lets
# bin/stale-owed-tickets.sh stop relying on an ssh append landing.
#READY_QUEUE_ROWS=0
#
# closeout_aged_table: "we already decided this build record is too old to page
# about" is the `closeout_aged` table instead of state/closeout-aged-out.tsv.
# The tsv is still written as the archive; the table is what survives losing it.
#CLOSEOUT_AGED_TABLE=0

